    "title": "Aurora Breaks Ground on $5.2M Dredging to Save Historic Mastodon Lake - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Richard M. Sullivan ,\n8 hours ago Aurora will break ground next Wednesday, Aug. 12, at 1 p.m. on a major dredging and shoreline restoration project at Mastodon Lake, the historic 28-acre pond at the heart of Phillips Park that has spent years silting up from stormwater runoff. The ceremony kicks off construction at the park, located at 1000 Ray Moses Drive, on a fix city officials say will dredge out decades of sediment and clean up the shoreline for good. Read full article\n1",
